  "title": "No-Bake Chocolate Peanut Butter Oat Bars",
  "blurb": "Quick energy bars made by mixing oats, cocoa and peanut butter, then pressing into a tin and chilling until firm.",
  "steps": [
    "Line a 20cm square tin with baking paper.",
    "Put the peanut butter and honey in a large bowl and stir together until smooth.",
    "Add the oats, cocoa powder, vanilla extract, pumpkin seeds and salt, then mix everything together until well combined.",
    "Tip the mixture into the prepared tin and press down firmly with the back of a spoon to create an even layer.",
    "Refrigerate for at least two hours until set, then cut into 12 bars."
